<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.mozilla.screencapture</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/cltbld/bin/capture-on-demand.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Fire the moment the harness writes the trigger file. This replaced
    StartInterval=1, which launchd throttled to its ~10s respawn floor because
    the helper exits almost instantly -- while the harness only waits 5s for the
    screenshot, producing empty / blank-desktop screenshots on Apple Silicon.
  -->
  <key>WatchPaths</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/cltbld/.trigger_screenshot</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    WatchPaths does NOT escape the respawn throttle -- switching away from
    StartInterval only moved the same 10s floor, it did not remove it. Measured
    on macmini-m4-80 (macOS 15) through the real trigger path: the first capture
    after load lands in ~0.3-0.5s, then EVERY subsequent capture is held at
    10.1-10.3s, because launchd applies ThrottleInterval (default 10s) to any
    job it relaunches, however that relaunch was triggered. Since the harness
    gives up at 5s, that means only the first failure screenshot per boot could
    ever arrive on time.

    Worse than a plain miss: the capture still happens ~10s later and lands at
    the path the harness asked for, so a screenshot does get uploaded -- just
    taken 10s after the fact, by which point the browser under test is often
    gone. That is a blank-desktop image from a capture that "succeeded", which
    is exactly the signature that survived the earlier WatchPaths change.

    Dropping the floor to 1s brings repeat captures to 1.1-1.35s (same host,
    same method), comfortably inside the harness window. 1 rather than 0 keeps a
    small floor as a runaway guard; screenshot requests are failure-driven and
    rare, so there is no meaningful respawn pressure either way.
  -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>1</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
